│    configured correctly.  This line sets the │
│    DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE environment        │
│    variable to point to your Django          │
│    project's settings module.  You must      │
│    replace 'your_project.settings' with the  │
│    actual path to your project's settings    │
│    file.  Without this, Django won't         │
│    initialize properly, and you'll get the   │
│    ImproperlyConfigured error.               │
│  • django.setup():  This line is essential   │
│    to initialize Django before using any     │
│    Django-related modules. It must be called │
│    after setting the DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE. │
│  • Added a general except Exception as e     │
│    block: This catches any other unexpected  │
│    errors during the test and prints the     │
│    stack trace before exiting with code 1.   │
│    This makes the test more robust.          │
│  • Removed unnecessary imports: The original │
