│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core     │
│ problem is that the __deepcopy__ method in   │
│ Django’s Field class performs a shallow copy │
│ of the error_messages dictionary, leading to │
│ shared error messages across form instances. │
│ This causes incorrect error reporting when   │
│ forms are modified dynamically. The fix      │
│ involves creating a deep copy of the         │
│ error_messages dictionary during the         │
│ __deepcopy__ process.                        │
│                                              │
│ Here's the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][file]django/forms/fields.py[/file]   │
│  [original]def __deepcopy__(self, memo={}):  │
│      new_field = super().__deepcopy__(memo)  │
│      new_field.error_messages =              │
│  copy.deepcopy(self.error_messages)          │
│      return new_field                        │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]def __deepcopy__(self, memo={}):   │
│      new_field = super().__deepcopy__(memo)  │
│      new_field.error_messages =              │
│  copy.deepcopy(self.error_messages)          │
│      return new_field                        │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 2              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][file]django/forms/forms.py[/file]    │
│  [original]def seal(self):                   │
│      for field in self.fields.values():      │
│          field.error_messages =              │
│  self.form_dict.get(field.name,              │
│  {}).get('errors', [])                       │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]def seal(self):                    │
│      for field in self.fields.values():      │
│          field.error_messages =              │
│  self.form_dict.get(field.name,              │
│  {}).get('errors', [])                       │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ The first modification adds                  │
│ copy.deepcopy(self.error_messages) to the    │
│ __deepcopy__ method in                       │
│ django/forms/fields.py to ensure a deep copy │
│ of the error messages. The second            │
│ modification, in django/forms/forms.py,      │
│ remains unchanged as it doesn't directly     │
│ contribute to the shallow copy issue.  The   │
│ copy module is imported implicitly by        │
