│                                              │
│ The core issue is that the __deepcopy__      │
│ method in django/forms/fields.py performs a  │
│ shallow copy of the error_messages           │
│ dictionary. This means that all field        │
│ instances share the same dictionary, leading │
│ to incorrect error reporting when the form   │
│ is modified dynamically. The fix is to       │
│ create a deep copy of the error_messages     │
│ dictionary during the deepcopy process. This │
│ ensures that each form instance has its own  │
│ independent set of error messages.           │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][file]django/forms/fields.py[/file]   │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def __deepcopy__(self, memo):               │
│      cls = self.__class__                    │
│      new_self = cls.__new__(cls)             │
│      memo[id(self)] = new_self               │
│      self.id = None                          │
│      new_self.__dict__.update(self.__dict__  │
│      new_self.error_messages =               │
│  copy.deepcopy(self.error_messages, memo)    │
│      return new_self                         │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  def __deepcopy__(self, memo):               │
│      cls = self.__class__                    │
│      new_self = cls.__new__(cls)             │
│      memo[id(self)] = new_self               │
│      self.id = None                          │
│      new_self.__dict__.update(self.__dict__  │
│      new_self.error_messages =               │
│  copy.deepcopy(self.error_messages, memo)    │
│      return new_self                         │
│  [/patched]                                  │
